c/core-ir.schema.json:2219:    \"ModelScope\": {\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json:2225:        \"templates\": {\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json:2267:        \"templates\",\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json:2277:    \"HistoryFamily\": {\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json:2561:        \"lower_attained\": {\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json:2571:        \"upper_attained\": {\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json:2629:        \"lower_attained\",\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json:2630:        \"upper_attained\",\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:120:precision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:124:available; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:132:an unknown rounding convention.\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:144:| roundMoney | Money<C>, Int, String -> Money<C>; only half_even supported in DemoDebt; rounding at posting boundary, rational ties exact |\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:158:A ModelScope lists templates, slots per entity/period, books, account roles,\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:161:nonnegative amount; inactive implies zero. A template declares both its posting\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:179:Money quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:190:attainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:263:family has a mean. Weighted runs preserve successful, unresolved and default\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:328:| reconstruct | IR, ModelScope, view, solver_lock, budgets | HistoryFamily and cell coverage, witnesses/conflicts/unknowns |\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:331:| bound | formula, query expression, domain, quantisation mode, solver/budget | certified bound/attainment or explicit Unknown/Unbounded |\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:377:  interval additionally needs the declared rounding convention; scale alone\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Deterministic reference checks for the design, not a product test suite.\n\nUses independently authored expectations and exact arithmetic. Z3 checks the\ndocument's supported rational-linear constraints; no statistical claim follows.\n\"\"\"\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom fractions import Fraction as Q\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport platform\nimport time\nimport z3\n\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nFIX=ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures'\nchecks=[]\n\ndef load(name): return json.loads((FIX/name).read_text())\ndef check(name, condition, detail):\n    checks.append(dict(name=name,passed=bool(condition),detail=detail))\n    if not condition: raise AssertionError(name+': '+str(detail))\n\ndef post(state, e, committed):\n    \"\"\"Local oracle for atomic double-entry/idempotency, deliberately small.\"\"\"\n    payload=json.dumps(e,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'))\n    if e['id'] in committed:\n        if committed[e['id']]!=payload: raise ValueError('EventIdentityConflict')\n        return\n    entries=[(p['account'],Q(p['signed_amount'])) for p in e['postings']]\n    if sum(v for _,v in entries)!=0: raise ValueError('UnbalancedBatch')\n    proposed=deepcopy(state)\n    for a,v in entries: proposed[a]+=v\n    state.clear(); state.update(proposed); committed[e['id']]=payload\n\ndef report_close(state, events, roles, period):\n    selected=[e for e in events if e['period']==period]\n    flows=defaultdict(Q)\n    for e in selected:\n        for p in e['postings']:\n            if p['account']=='cash' and e['cash_class']:\n                flows[e['cash_class']]+=Q(p['signed_amount'])\n    profit=-sum(v for a,v in state.items() if roles[a] in ['income','expense'])\n    revenue=-state['revenue']\n    interest,tax=state['interest'],state['tax']\n    # Closing is independent of the event generator; no cash arises here.\n    for a in list(state):\n        if roles[a] in ['income','expense']:\n            state['retained']+=state[a];state[a]=Q(0)\n    result=dict(cash=state['cash'],receivables=state['receivables'],inventory=state['inventory'],\n        plant_net=state['plant_cost']+state['accum_depreciation'],tax_prepaid=state['tax_prepaid'],\n        assets=sum(v for a,v in state.items() if roles[a] in ['asset','contra_asset']),\n        payables=-state['payables'],debt=-state['debt'],\n        equity=-sum(v for a,v in state.items() if roles[a]=='equity'),\n        revenue=revenue,profit=profit,interest=interest,tax=tax,\n        operating_cash=flows['operating'],investing_cash=flows['investing'],financing_cash=flows['financing'])\n    check('balanced_'+period,sum(state.values())==0 and result['assets']==result['payables']+result['debt']+result['equity'],str(result))\n    return result\n\ndef compare(name,actual,expected):\n    check(name,all(actual[k]==Q(v) for k,v in expected.items()),{k:str(actual[k]) for k in expected})\n\ndef corporate():\n    f=load('northstar.json'); state=defaultdict(Q,{k:Q(v) for k,v in f['opening'].items()}); committed={}\n    check('opening_balance',sum(state.values())==0,'Signed account total is zero')\n    periods={}\n    for period in ['2024H1','2024H2']:\n        for e in f['historical_events']:\n            if e['period']==period:post(state,e,committed)\n        periods[period]=report_close(state,f['historical_events'],f['accounts'],period)\n        compare(period,periods[period],f['expected'][period])\n    annual={k:sum(r[k] for r in periods.values()) for k in ['revenue','profit','operating_cash','investing_cash','financing_cash']}\n    annual['cash_change']=state['cash']-Q(f['opening']['cash'])\n    compare('annual_statements',annual,f['expected']['2024FY'])\n    # Inverse construction from observed bridges. F,V remain a joint family.\n    sales,collection,purchase,payment,cost,F,V=z3.Reals('sales collection purchase payment cost F V')\n    constraints=[sales==260,35==20+sales-collection,20==30+purchase-cost,\n        30==20+purchase-payment,cost==165,F>=0,V>=0,F+V==100,QZ('0.05')*(F+V)==5]\n    solver=z3.Solver();solver.add(*constraints)\n    check('reconstruction_feasible',solver.check()==z3.sat,'Closed scope annual bridge family')\n    for x,value in [(collection,245),(purchase,155),(payment,145)]:\n        solver.push();solver.add(x!=value); r=solver.check();solver.pop()\n        check('recovered_'+str(x),r==z3.unsat,str(value))\n    for fixed in [0,25,100]:\n        solver.push();solver.add(F==fixed);r=solver.check();solver.pop()\n        check('family_retains_fixed_'+str(fixed),r==z3.sat,'Different exposures with same historical interest')\n    solver.push();solver.add(F==101);r=solver.check();solver.pop()\n    check('impossible_debt_mix_rejected',r==z3.unsat,'Nonnegative floating amount forbids F=101')\n    forecast=f['forecast']\n    for branch,interest in [('fixed',Q(5)),('floating',Q(7))]:\n        s=deepcopy(state); events=[]\n        def e(name,entries,cls=None):\n            record=dict(id='2025.'+name,period='2025_'+branch,date='2025-12-31',cash_class=cls,\n                        postings=[dict(account=a,signed_amount=str(v)) for a,v in entries])\n            events.append(record); post(s,record,{})\n        demand=Q(forecast['demand_units']);price=Q(forecast['price']);cost=Q(forecast['unit_cost'])\n        purchases=(demand+Q(forecast['target_inventory_units'])-s['inventory']/cost)*cost\n        sales=demand*price; cogs=demand*cost\n        collections=Q(forecast['current_sales_collection_fraction'])*sales+Q(forecast['legacy_receivable_collections'])\n        suppliers=Q(forecast['old_payables_paid'])+Q(forecast['new_purchases_paid'])\n        depreciation=Q(10)+Q(10)/5+Q(12)/12\n        tax=(sales-cogs-Q(forecast['payroll'])-depreciation-interest)*Q(forecast['tax_rate'])\n        e('sale',[('receivables',sales),('revenue',-sales)])\n        e('collect',[('cash',collections),('receivables',-collections)],'operating')\n        e('purchase',[('inventory',purchases),('payables',-purchases)])\n        e('supplier',[('payables',suppliers),('cash',-suppliers)],'operating')\n        e('deliver',[('cost_of_sales',cogs),('inventory',-cogs)])\n        e('payroll',[('payroll',50),('cash',-50)],'operating')\n        e('capex',[('plant_cost',20),('cash',-20)],'investing')\n        e('depreciate',[('depreciation',depreciation),('accum_depreciation',-depreciation)])\n        e('interest',[('interest',interest),('cash',-interest)],'operating')\n        e('tax',[('tax',tax),('cash',-tax)],'operating')\n        e('dividend',[('retained',8),('cash',-8)],'financing')\n        result=report_close(s,events,f['accounts'],'2025_'+branch)\n        compare('forecast_'+branch,result,f['expected']['2025_'+branch])\n        check('direct_indirect_cash_'+branch,\n              result['operating_cash']==result['profit']+depreciation-(s['receivables']-state['receivables'])-(s['inventory']-state['inventory'])-(s['payables']-state['payables']),\n              'Profit + noncash depreciation - asset increases + liability increases')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' MISSION_CONTROL.md; sed -n '1,55p' docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md; sed -n '1,55p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; rg -n '\"'^##.*G(1|3|15|16)'\"\\\\b|\"'^'\"\\\\| G(1|3|15|16) ' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util,json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nprint('P04 files', [(str(p),p.exists()) for p in [Path('tests/test_accounting_p04.py'),Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/conformance.json'),Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/result.md')]])\ns=importlib.util.find_spec('z3');print('z3',s.origin if s else None)\np=Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03')\nprint('structured records',[str(f) for f in p.glob('*.json') if 'review' in f.name or 'check' in f.name])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' MISSION_CONTROL.md; sed -n '1,55p' docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md; sed -n '1,55p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; rg -n '\"'^##.*G(1|3|15|16)'\"\\\\b|\"'^'\"\\\\| G(1|3|15|16) ' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util,json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nprint('P04 files', [(str(p),p.exists()) for p in [Path('tests/test_accounting_p04.py'),Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/conformance.json'),Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/result.md')]])\ns=importlib.util.find_spec('z3');print('z3',s.origin if s else None)\np=Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03')\nprint('structured records',[str(f) for f in p.glob('*.json') if 'review' in f.name or 'check' in f.name])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# AccDSL mission control\n\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong) at the user's request.\nStatus: active mission; Version 1.2 is a repaired design candidate with checked\nreference cases. Full product, domain and human acceptance remain pending.\n\n## Purpose\n\nDesign a system that represents a company's historical financial disclosures,\npreserves economically different histories and interpretations compatible with\nthe evidence, and carries those alternatives into scenario-dependent future\njournals and financial statements. Preserve their separate conditional outcome\ndistributions or feasible sets, including uncertainty that cannot be assigned\ndefensible probabilities.\n\nThe immediate deliverable is a detailed, readable LaTeX product and method\ndesign, with compiled PDF, supporting literature and software investigation,\nprecise implementation contracts and acceptance examples. The eventual product\nis the working representation and simulation engine. A document build, a small\nfinancing example and an implemented prototype are different achievements.\n\n## Authority and origin\n\nThis mission records the user's existing directions; it does not replace new\nuser instructions or higher-priority instructions. The three original requests\nare preserved in saved session `01a0f8e0-0c0b-7332-8f7e-d6b93ce32761`, at JSONL\nrecords 10, 115 and 145. They establish whole-company history, heterogeneous\naccounting, preservation of alternative journals/outcomes, a broad literature\nand software survey, and an implementation-governing LaTeX document. The current\nrequest establishes this durable mission and a requirements-based gap audit.\n\nThe user's subsequent direction establishes MC35: complete feasible internal\npreparation before paying for professional review. The user supplied a planning\nrate of US$500–1,200/hour. This work order is binding; no estimated savings or\nprofessional engagement is inferred from it.\n\nThe [requirements register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\ndistinguishes direct user requirements from policy obligations and engineering\nrequirements derived from those goals. Python, storage engines, parser design,\nsolver libraries and a particular first-company example remain replaceable\nimplementation proposals. Designing a DSL is part of the work; claiming it is\nbetter than all alternatives is not a predetermined conclusion.\n\n## Main goals\n\n| Goal | Required outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| M1 — Represent the historical record | Preserve annual, quarterly and semi-annual statements, notes, policies and relevant referenced disclosures, with their source, context, temporal meaning and unresolved content. |\n| M2 — Preserve alternative explanations | Represent joint families of admissible histories, journal movements, contract states and interpretations; distinguish absent facts, accounting choices, estimates and future randomness. |\n| M3 — Simulate financial evolution | Apply explicit economic scenarios and behaviour to economic state, generate admissible journal entries, and produce coherent future statements and conditional results. |\n| M4 — Handle accounting and sector diversity | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE, industry and company differences, group boundaries, banks, insurers, liabilities, capital, bonds and equity. |\n| M5 — Specify implementable methods and language | Define reconstruction, accounting, inference and execution procedures, types, IR, DSL, interfaces, failure behaviour and persistence precisely enough for compatible implementations. |\n| M6 — Ground choices in research and reusable tools | Inspect primary literature beyond the existing collection and official software, archive relevant sources, compare credible alternatives and document justified inclusion/exclusion and reuse decisions. |\n| M7 — Deliver the governing design | Produce one rigorous, understandable LaTeX/PDF argument with complete worked cases, explicit scope, source support, method details and an implementation sequence. |\n| M8 — Establish evidence and maintain direction | Define conformance and release evidence, preserve reproducibility, keep engineering/accounting/scientific conclusions separate, and maintain requirements and open decisions as work proceeds. |\n\n## Requirements that must survive every implementation choice\n\n1. Source preservation is broader than numerical extraction. Account for all\n   source material within the declared disclosure package, including notes and\n   cross-references. Content that cannot yet be formalised stays visible with\n   a reason; it is not silently excluded from a completeness claim.\n2. Preserve reported assertions, derived consequences and modelling assumptions\n   separately. A missing value is not zero; a reported number is not automatic\n   proof of the underlying economic state. Source conflicts remain inspectable.\n3. Carry entity, group perimeter, concept, dimensions, units, currency, basis,\n   precision and time through every calculation. Label mapping does not itself\n   convert between accounting standards. Avoid double counting overlapping\n   classifications.\n4. Preserve original and revised information. Economic time, reporting periods,\n   availability/publication and system ingestion/version time answer different\n   questions. Historical forecasts cannot use later evidence inadvertently.\n5. Keep alternatives jointly consistent across statements, notes, dates,\n   contracts and accounts. Include economic state beyond journals: identical\n   historical postings can conceal different future exposures.\n6. Every reconstructed family has an explicit model scope and completeness\n   status. A selected witness, bounded search or convenient aggregate cannot be\n   presented as all real histories. Scope exclusions remain mission limitations.\n7. Preserve conditional results by explanation and scenario. A set or interval\n   does not become a probability distribution without a declared measure. No\n   weights from representation counts, arbitrary equality or LLM confidence.\n   Keep dependence between statement amounts and through time.\n8. Generate events from explicit contract and behavioural assumptions, then\n   apply recognition/measurement and posting rules. Balanced journals are\n   necessary but do not prove accounting treatment or economic correctness.\n9. Treat unsupported calculations, unresolved branches, numerical failure and\n   economically meaningful default as distinct outcomes. Do not silently drop\n   failed branches, manufacture financing or report sampled extrema as exact\n   bounds.\n10. Compare a DSL with credible alternatives on the same tasks, especially the\n    typed-library/shared-IR baseline. Reuse software where its inspected\n    capabilities fit, with explicit adapter contracts and limits.\n11. Support imported technical claims with inspected primary sections and local\n    copies. Preserve relevant papers under `docs/papers` using\n    `Title First-author-surname (year).pdf`; preserve the original collection.\n    Technical reading, actual literature screening and source corrections must\n    be recorded, not inferred from metadata or generated status labels.\n12. Make assumptions, derivations, scope and limits understandable in the\n    manuscript itself. Full company cases and precise expected outputs must\n    connect the concepts to implementation. Page count and polished prose are\n    not substitutes for these requirements.\n\n## What counts as completion\n\nThe [requirement register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\ndefines evidence needed for MC01–MC35. Each requirement must have an identified\ndocument location, stated behaviour/method, a suitable worked case or other\ncheck, and an honest assessment. A mention is `partial`; promised future work\nis `open`; a precise design is `specified`; checked evidence can support\n`checked` within its stated scope. `Not checked` is never silently converted\n# Accounting master checkpoint\n\nUpdated: 3 October 2026 (Hong Kong), under the user's create/review/execute instruction.\nThe executable catalog covers G1–G18 while retaining MC01–MC35 unchanged.\n\n## Resume entry point\n\nRun this exact command, without shell wrappers or environment prefixes:\n\n```text\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py run\n```\n\nRead the saved state and next plan alongside this completed-run checkpoint:\n\n- ../../data/accounting-master/state.json\n- ../../data/accounting-master/next-plan.md\n- ../../data/accounting-master/events.jsonl\n- ../../data/accounting-master/runs/\n- accounting-master-program.md\n- ../design/review/accounting-master-review.md\n\n## Completed run and continuation\n\nRun `20261002T205123-6b8e9a16` finished at 22:08:22 UTC on 2 October\n(06:08:22 Hong Kong on 3 October) with outcome `wall_limit` and exit code 2.\nIts configured limit was 4,700 seconds. The child record is `finished`, with\nno recorded or independently observed surviving group members. No master run\nis active. The final next-plan generation is 43 and its state hash matches the\nsaved state. This is a resumable budget boundary, not mission completion.\n\n| Phase | Actual outcome | Evidence and remaining work |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| P00/P01 | Accepted internally; retained from earlier execution | Baseline and 192 source-context records remain hash-valid. Source availability, semantics and annotations retain their existing limits. |\n| P02 | Accepted internally at 21:41:34 UTC | 13 annual and 10 interim note dispositions, 125 observations, 34 selected reconciliations and 698 anchors; all 20 supervisor tests passed. The final read-only reviewer returned AGREE and exited cleanly in 237.155 seconds. |\n| P03 | `needs_repair`; partial implementation retained | Real parsing/binding/lowering, typed input, semantic repairs, checker and required reports are present. Post-run verification passed 9 test methods covering 85 catalogued obligations, but no completed implementation response, supervisor phase checks or result review was obtained after the last repair. |\n| P08 | `needs_repair`; not attempted in this run | Earlier planning interruption remains to be resumed. It is independently eligible alongside P03. |\n| P04–P07/P09–P14 | Pending | Dependencies and original accounting, execution, benchmark, forecasting and manuscript obligations remain open. |\n\nP02's 18 accepted evidence hashes match. They include no unrelated P03 or\ncontroller edits. Its first two result-review processes timed out; the second\nalso wrote an AGREE response, which was correctly not accepted from a timed-out\nprocess. The final review inspected the code and source evidence, reran 18\ntests successfully, and relied on the matching supervisor 20-test record for\ntwo temporary-file tests that its read-only environment could not run. Historical\nworker text saying “acceptance pending” or “submit for review” is superseded by\nthe final clean review and accepted state. Full note/agreement semantics,\nhistorical availability, unidentified histories, accounting/forecast validity\nand human acceptance remain unresolved.\n\nP03's repair added rejection of missing assumptions/mappings, disconnected\nmodel/package/scope references and other semantic corruptions. Its worker\ntimed out after updating the reports; the next attempt could not start within\nthe remaining run budget. The generated PASS is bounded author conformance\nevidence, not accepted phase status. The post-run verification is newer than\n# Active checkpoint\n\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\n\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\n\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\n\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\n\nThe collector checkpoints each attempt and supports `--revalidate-retained`,\n`--resolved-only`, sequential `--index-plan` capture and bounded host failures.\nOfficial HSBC and Midea archives, SAIC year pages, Ping An's published report\nfeed, SEC submissions and issuer-hosted US filing feeds have been resolved.\nDirect SEC archive downloads returned 403; issuer-hosted copies are used with\nthe regulator identity and filing dates retained. Run one acquisition writer\nat a time. The optional `--http-client curl` bounds total request time;\n`--source-host` can select a resolved alternate without retrying known failures.\nPing An's last ASBE slot was filled by an A-share report attachment on a public\nmirror; the distinct IFRS copy remains excluded from that slot. Do not reset\nthe ledger, initialise Git or promote source checks into accounting evidence.\n\nThe next internal work is task-specific literal/context/span annotation and\nCore 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\nexisting fixtures. `benchmark-protocol-v1.json` and\n`annotation-record.schema.json` define the proposed tasks and exchange format;\nissuer-family roles are provisional, with no model score or gold labels.\nResolve incorporated documents, revisions and publication timing before\nhistorical forecasting. Publication dates are unverified for 136 of 192\naccepted reports; 56 have filing-date metadata. No paid review is triggered.\n\n## Current deliverable\n\n`docs/design/accounting-product-design.pdf` and its LaTeX sources are Version\n1.2, a 79-page design candidate with 11 chapters and two appendices. It contains\ncomplete Northstar annual/interim/revision/forecast cases, an Apple filing\ninventory and conditional financing stress, historical construction and solver\nlimits, corporate operations, sector examples, Core 0 contracts,\nreview/replay/adapter definitions and corpus/release protocols.\n\nThe 8 mission goals and MC01–MC34 retain their requirement and acceptance\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:47:### G1. Reconstruction defines the answer more precisely than the algorithm\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:119:### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:138:### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\nP04 files [('tests/test_accounting_p04.py', False), ('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/conformance.json', False), ('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/result.md', False)]\nz3 /home/chakwong/miniconda3/envs/tfgpu/lib/python3.11/site-packages/z3/__init__.py\nstructured records ['data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03/review_plan-0.response.json', 'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03/review_plan-0.recovery.json', 'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03/review_plan-0.process.json']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"P03 preserves history families as unsearched; the older reference checks enter final constraint equations directly. P04 therefore needs a construction layer. Z3 is already installed, so the plan can use exact rational solving without adding a dependency. Tests will need to check input-to-constraint construction separately from solver results."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '112,204p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '244,270p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '320,338p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '1435,1480p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py; sed -n '2090,2130p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '112,204p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '244,270p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '320,338p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '1435,1480p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py; sed -n '2090,2130p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"`simpleInterest(principal,rate,fraction)` explicitly. Integer counts stay integer.\nDivision by a symbolic value\nrequires nonzero proof and is outside the rational-linear solver fragment.\n\nContext equality compares entity, perimeter version, measurement basis,\ncurrency/unit, instant/period/calendar and dimensions. A sum may discard a\ndimension only through a valid partition mapping. Reference fields and source\nspans may differ without changing financial comparability. Observation\nprecision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\nis an unresolved reading, not an assumed half-unit interval.\n\nDomain `display` preserves the disclosed spelling, unit/scale and sign when\navailable; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\nan unrounded mathematical symbol. The SourceSpan retains the original text.\nAn exact numeric domain has equal closed bounds; an interval has ordered bounds\nand explicit endpoint inclusion (a null endpoint is unbounded and open).\nFinite-domain `values` are distinct typed expression IDs and use null bounds.\nA missing domain has null bounds, no values, and a non-null `missing_reason`;\nother domain kinds have null `missing_reason`. Empty or contradictory admitted\ndomains return an explicit consistency error. Display text alone never supplies\nan unknown rounding convention.\n\nThe complete built-in set is:\n\n| Name | Signature and effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| external | String -> SourceRef; resolves a frozen registry key; never fetches network content during evaluation |\n| value | Observation<T> -> contextual T or shared constrained Symbol<T>; missing raises MissingEvidence |\n| constant | T -> dated exogenous Driver<T>, all dates in the explicit scenario horizon |\n| simpleInterest | Money<C>, Rate<annual_simple>, YearFraction -> Money<C>, exact product; symbolic classification happens after expansion |\n| yearFraction | start, end, CalendarRef, ConventionRef -> YearFraction; supported conventions `one_year` and `half_year_fixture` require exact named periods; others require a registered calculator |\n| currencyScale | CurrencyRef -> Int from the frozen currency registry, USD=2 in demonstration |\n| roundMoney | Money<C>, Int, String -> Money<C>; only half_even supported in DemoDebt; rounding at posting boundary, rational ties exact |\n| sumOver | PartitionRef, array of contextual T -> contextual T with that dimension removed; disjoint/exhaustive population proof required |\n| convert | Money<C1>, Measurement<Rate<C2/C1>> -> Money<C2>; valuation date and purpose must match, source amount retained |\n| balance | StateRef, AccountRef -> signed Money<C>; read-only committed state at information date |\n\nAll other functions must have a package-registered pure signature and versioned\nimplementation digest; their capability is explicit. Rules may bind values,\ncheck requirements and propose postings. They cannot sample, mutate state or\naccess I/O. Contract and behaviour plugins produce proposed events/state\nchanges through the typed interfaces below. Zero-posting contract changes need\nan explicit non-recognition operation.\n\n## Reconstruction model and finite coverage\n\nA ModelScope lists templates, slots per entity/period, books, account roles,\ntiming/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\noperations. A slot is a possible aggregate event, with an active flag and\nnonnegative amount; inactive implies zero. A template declares both its posting\nincidence vector and economic-state change. Sales and collections are different\nslots; issue and reset are different slots. Debt states retain F/V, rates,\nreset calendar, maturity and hedge links even when historical incidence agrees.\n\nInstantiate every declared slot once, then share variables by economic IDs and\nobservation IDs. Compile roll-forwards and report mappings into constraints;\nadd each accepted evidence domain once. Match source observations by exact\ncontext/mapping, never by label similarity. Attach source/assumption IDs to\nconstraints. Branch on finite choices only, with mutually exclusive guards;\ncontinuous families remain formulas. Count completed, infeasible and unresolved\nchoice cells. `ExactWithinScope` requires every cell decided and each matching\nsource obligation resolved or explicitly outside simulation scope. A satisfied\nwitness alone does not establish coverage. Real-world completeness is never\ninferred from this finite result.\n\nSupported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\nbounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\nMoney quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\nminor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\nand nonlinear constraints may not be silently submitted as continuous LPs.\nUnknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\nfunctions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\nFixed proportions times known totals are linear; variable F,V with F+V=D is\nlinear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\nproved D>0 becomes F>=aD; an unknown a restores bilinearity.\n\nFeasibility results are sat+exact witness, unsat+constraint/source core or\nunknown+reason+undecided formula. Bounds include lower/upper rational value,\nattainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ninequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\nunknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\ntimeout preserves undecided cells rather than deleting them.\n\n## Temporal selection and local review\n\nAn EvidenceView first filters by availability cutoff and (if requested)\ningestion cutoff. Day-only availability maps to the next local midnight using\nthe named timezone; finer availability requires evidence. Selective explicit\nsupersession removes only the targeted assertions in the same context. A\nsuperseding assertion must be eligible itself. Transitive successors follow\nthe acyclic supersession graph. Competing maximal assertions form a conflict\nset, never a last-row-wins result. Original view chooses initial assertions in\neach chain from a declared filing, not arbitrary earliest ingestion. A filing\nspecified equations in a named acyclic structural model, retaining exogenous\nnoise; absence of that model yields UnsupportedScenario. Risk-neutral pricing\nand real-world simulation measures have different IDs and cannot be mixed\nwithout an explicit justified transformation.\n\nInformationView(date, observer, role, evidence_view, committed_prefix,\nannounced_scenario_inputs, forecast_model) exposes past/current facts and\npermitted forecasts. Future realised innovations and future event outcomes\nare unavailable. A scenario may announce an entire stress path to management\nonly when its visibility is `announced`; otherwise management sees current and\npast driver values. Valuation uses an inner expectation conditional on this\nview, with an independent stream domain from outer realised defaults.\n\nRunResult preserves rows by hypothesis/continuous condition, scenario, path and\ndate. Cells carry Context and Exact/Symbolic/Samples/CertifiedBounds/ExploredRange/\nUnresolved tags. Path failure has an enum: EconomicDefault, Unsupported,\nNumericalFailure, SolverUnknown, Cancelled. Default retains the legal obligations\nand usable state; an unsupported required treatment stops affected descendants.\nUnaffected outputs may survive through the dependency graph. No unweighted\nfamily has a mean. Weighted runs preserve successful, unresolved and default\nmass; missing outcomes block unconditional means/quantiles. Conditional-on-success\nresults require an explicit separate request and show their denominator.\n\nFinite joint measures attach to disjoint economic hypotheses, not alternative\nlabels. Overlapping views cannot be summed; reparameterisations require a\npushforward measure, with Jacobian where densities are used. Priors and\nlikelihoods list information blocks so totals/components do not duplicate\npath, retryable, capability). No method modifies its inputs. A request_id makes\nmutating import/review operations idempotent. The normative operations are:\n\n| Operation | Required arguments | Success |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ingest | bytes/hash, filing_id, availability, extractor_lock, request_id | SourceDocument, source units, proposed readings, coverage obligations |\n| review | reading_ids, action, evidence, reviewer, reason, prior_view, request_id | ReviewDecision, new EvidenceView, invalidated descendants |\n| compile | source/typed-IR, schema_version, package_lock, evidence_view | validated IR, unresolved simulation inputs, diagnostic list |\n| reconstruct | IR, ModelScope, view, solver_lock, budgets | HistoryFamily and cell coverage, witnesses/conflicts/unknowns |\n| simulate | family/conditions, initial_state, scenarios, horizon, InformationPolicy, packages, numeric and stream settings, outputs, budgets | RunResult with committed state/journals and branch manifest |\n| report | committed run/date/period, mapping, view, queries | contextual joint cells and explanation references |\n| bound | formula, query expression, domain, quantisation mode, solver/budget | certified bound/attainment or explicit Unknown/Unbounded |\n| explain | output_id, frozen run_id | typed dependency graph, no latest-source substitution |\n| replay | run_id, checkpoint_id, lock/environment | equal exact outputs or explicit numerical comparison report |\n\nContract methods are schedule(terms,start,end,calendar), observe(terms,date,info),\npayoff(terms,event,state,market), transition(state,event). Behaviour is\ndecide(state,information,policy) -> actions. Measurement is measure(state,event,\ninformation,method) -> value/basis/error/method annotations. Accounting is\n        if total != 0:\n            self.fail(\"UnbalancedState\", \"opening signed balances must sum to zero\", opening_decl.name)\n        self.ir[\"states\"].append({\"id\": opening_decl.name, \"date\": _iso(opening.date, opening_decl.name),\n                                   \"book\": opening_decl.book,\n                                   \"balances\": [{\"account\": name, \"signed_amount\": rational(value)} for name, value in opening.balances],\n                                   \"contracts\": [contract.name], \"measurements\": [],\n                                   \"dependencies\": list(opening.dependencies) or [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][2]]})\n        report = next(iter(self.reports.values()))\n        rb = self.bindings.report(report.mapping.key if isinstance(report.mapping, External) else str(report.mapping)) if isinstance(report.mapping, External) else None\n        if rb is None:\n            self.fail(\"UnsupportedReportMapping\", \"report mapping must be an explicit external binding\", report.name)\n        self.ir[\"reportMappings\"].append({\"id\": report.name, \"book\": report.book, \"basis\": package.id,\n                                          \"rows\": [{\"name\": \"package_mapping\", \"expression\": self._source_ref_expr(rb.mapping, report.name)}],\n                                          \"closing_policy\": f\"{package.id}/{rb.closing_policy}\",\n                                          \"cash_flow_policy\": f\"{package.id}/{rb.cash_flow_policy}\",\n                                          \"required_operations\": [f\"{package.id}/{x}\" for x in rb.required_operations]})\n        # Profile scope and conservative family status.  This profile does not\n        # perform a reconstruction or feasibility search.\n        slot = self._literal_expr(\"scope\", \"slot_limit\", 1, \"Int\")\n        self.ir[\"modelScopes\"].append({\"id\": model_scope, \"templates\": [f\"{package.id}/{contract.type_name}\"],\n                                       \"slot_limits\": [{\"name\": \"debt_contracts\", \"expression\": slot}],\n                                       \"resolution\": \"one fixed/floating aggregate, annual simple accrual\",\n                                       \"calendars\": [self.bindings.calendar_id], \"choices\": [],\n                                       \"exclusions\": [\"fees\", \"foreign_currency\", \"embedded_options\"], \"obligations\": []})\n        family_id = f\"history:{_clean_id(self.model_id)}\"\n        self.ir[\"historyFamilies\"].append({\"id\": family_id, \"scope\": model_scope,\n            \"evidence_view\": evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][2], \"opening_state\": opening_decl.name,\n            \"symbols\": list(self.symbols), \"choices\": [], \"constraints\": constraint_ids,\n            \"alternatives\": alt_ids, \"feasibility\": \"Unknown\", \"coverage\": \"PartialSearch\",\n            \"completed_cells\": 0, \"unresolved_cells\": 1, \"witnesses\": [], \"solver_results\": []})\n        declarations = [self.let_ids.get(n, n) for n in self.decls]\n        declarations = [n for n in declarations if n not in self.sources]\n        self.ir[\"models\"].append({\"id\": self.model_id, \"language_version\": \"Core0.1\",\n                                  \"declarations\": list(dict.fromkeys(declarations)),\n                                  \"package_lock\": [package.id], \"scope\": model_scope})\n        self.ir[\"expressions\"] = list(self.expr_rows.values())\n        self.ir[\"diagnostics\"] = []\n        # Evidence view observations were added after creation; record all\n        # generated rows deterministically.\n        self.ir[\"sourceSpans\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n        self.ir[\"documents\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n        self.ir[\"observations\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n        self.ir[\"expressions\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n        self.ir[\"assumptions\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n        self.ir[\"constraints\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n        self.ir[\"alternatives\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n    if (model[\"scope\"] != scope[\"id\"] or family[\"scope\"] != scope[\"id\"] or\n            model[\"package_lock\"] != [p.id for p in bindings.packages] or\n            model[\"language_version\"] != \"Core0.1\"):\n        raise _diag(\"ModelBinding\", \"model scope or package lock is inconsistent\", model[\"id\"])\n    declarations = model[\"declarations\"]\n    required = {r[\"id\"] for k in (\"entities\", \"books\", \"accounts\", \"states\", \"observations\",\n                \"symbols\", \"contracts\", \"alternatives\", \"scenarios\", \"reportMappings\") for r in ir[k]}\n    if (len(declarations) != len(set(declarations)) or not required.issubset(declarations)\n            or any(name not in nodes for name in declarations)):\n        raise _diag(\"ModelBinding\", \"model declarations are missing or unresolved\", model[\"id\"])\n    if (scope[\"templates\"] != [ir[\"contracts\"][0][\"type\"]] or\n            scope[\"calendars\"] != [bindings.calendar_id] or scope[\"choices\"] or\n            scope[\"obligations\"] or scope[\"exclusions\"] != [\"fees\", \"foreign_currency\", \"embedded_options\"] or\n            len(scope[\"slot_limits\"]) != 1 or scope[\"slot_limits\"][0][\"name\"] != \"debt_contracts\" or\n            checker.expr(scope[\"slot_limits\"][0][\"expression\"]) != (\"Int\", None, Fraction(1))):\n        raise _diag(\"ScopeBinding\", \"scope differs from supported debt profile\", scope[\"id\"])\n    if family[\"choices\"]:\n        raise _diag(\"UnsupportedProfile\", \"finite choices are outside Core0.1\", family[\"id\"])\n    alternatives = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"alternatives\"]}\n    if not alternatives:\n        raise _diag(\"ProfileCardinality\", \"at least one alternative is required\", \"alternatives\")\n    expected_assumptions = []\n    for row in ir[\"constraints\"]:\n        if row[\"scope\"] not in set(alternatives) | {scope[\"id\"]} or row[\"kind\"] != \"assumption\":\n            raise _diag(\"ConstraintScope\", \"constraint has unsupported scope or kind\", row[\"id\"])\n        expected_assumptions.append((row[\"scope\"], row[\"expression\"]))\n    for alt in alternatives.values():\n        expected = {c[\"id\"] for c in ir[\"constraints\"] if c[\"scope\"] == alt[\"id\"]}\n        if set(alt[\"constraints\"]) != expected or len(alt[\"constraints\"]) != len(expected):\n            raise _diag(\"AlternativeScope\", \"branch has lost or duplicate conditions\", alt[\"id\"])\n    for row in ir[\"contracts\"]:\n        expected_assumptions.extend((row[\"id\"], f[\"expression\"]) for f in row[\"fields\"]\n                                    if f[\"name\"] in {\"fixed_rate\", \"initial_floating_rate\"})\n    for row in ir[\"scenarios\"]:\n        if (row[\"kind\"] != \"ExogenousStress\" or row[\"visibility\"] != \"announced\" or\n                row[\"probability_model\"] is not None or row[\"observed_event\"] is not None or\n                row[\"structural_model\"] is not None or row[\"replaced_equations\"] or\n                len(row[\"drivers\"]) != 1 or row[\"drivers\"][0][\"name\"] != \"market_rate\"):\n            raise _diag(\"ScenarioFields\", \"scenario differs from supported exogenous stress\", row[\"id\"])\n        expected_assumptions.append((row[\"id\"], row[\"drivers\"][0][\"expression\"]))\n    actual_assumptions = [(a[\"scope\"], a[\"expression\"]) for a in ir[\"assumptions\"]]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '47,70p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '98,118p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '119,157p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '126,178p' scripts/check_repair_conformance.py; cat data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03/review_plan-0.response.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '47,70p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '98,118p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '119,157p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '126,178p' scripts/check_repair_conformance.py; cat data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03/review_plan-0.response.json\"","aggregated_output":"### G1. Reconstruction defines the answer more precisely than the algorithm\n\nEvidence: [historical compatibility](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:12)\nand [reconstruction procedure](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:28).\n\nThe feasible-history set is defined relative to model scope M. The procedure\nsays to build variables, add supported bridges and contract constraints, solve,\nand retain alternatives. It leaves the critical translation from actual\ndisclosures to that model largely unspecified: which event and contract\ntemplates are available, how their instances are proposed, how account/note\nmappings become joint constraints, how structural alternatives are generated,\nand what coverage can be asserted after bounded search. Limits on event types,\ntime resolution and latent contracts are acknowledged but not instantiated in\na reference scope.\n\nConsequence: two implementations can both satisfy the prose while constructing\nmaterially different feasible families. An omitted floating-rate structure can\nremove a rate-sensitive future without violating any balance identity.\n\nRequired repair: specify one bounded reference model, its template registry,\ncandidate-generation procedure, constraint lowering, scope exclusions,\nsufficient-state checks and partial-search semantics. Include exact examples\nof an admissible history retained, an incompatible history rejected, and an\neconomically relevant possibility outside the declared scope. A solver witness\n### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\n\nEvidence: [linear core scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:247),\n[debt decomposition](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:104),\nand [rounded observations](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:131).\n\nThe example deliberately makes debt exactly 100. In a real rounded disclosure,\nlet D denote the shared unknown debt amount and alpha the unknown fixed\nfraction. Its expression for fixed principal becomes alpha times D. This is\nbilinear because both factors are unknown, although the supported core is\nlinear. Posting quantisation, symbolic applicability and simultaneous funding\nrelations introduce further boundaries between symbolic representation and\ncertified computation. Unsupported-operation diagnostics are specified, but a\ncomplete lowering or approximation policy is not.\n\nRequired repair: enumerate supported formula classes and solver operations,\nincluding rounding, strict bounds and attainment. Where valid, use a linear\nparameterisation: fixed amount F and floating amount V, with F+V=D and F,V\nnonnegative; then future interest at known rates is linear in F and V. Specify\nwhen that rewrite is equivalent to the intended model and when additional\nfraction restrictions prevent it. Unsupported cases must retain the model and\n### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\n\nRequirements: MC04, MC08, MC10, MC12, MC24. Refines G1, G2 and G6.\nEvidence: [interpretation distinction](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:67)\nand [alternative records](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:183).\n\nAn unknown fixed-rate share, two readings of a note, a permitted accounting\nelection, a measurement estimate and a future management decision are different\nuncertainties. The text recognises this, but generic symbols/choices and\nassumption provenance do not fully specify how each kind is validated,\nupdated or propagated. An unsupported treatment must not be accepted as an\nequally legitimate interpretation merely because it produces balanced entries.\n\nRequired evidence: define these distinctions in the model and review contracts,\nincluding links between dependent uncertainties. Show an admissible alternative,\nan evidence-refuted alternative and an unsupported accounting treatment.\nPreserve a possibly erroneous source assertion as evidence without silently\nendorsing its treatment. This requires no new fraud-detection product.\n\n### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\n\nRequirements: MC11, MC22. Refines G1 and G6.\nEvidence: [conditional-law equivalence](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:222).\n\nThe definition that grouped histories must have the same relevant conditional\nlaws is useful. It does not supply a usable rule for choosing instrument,\nlot, vintage or cohort resolution, carrying necessary accounting memory, or\nreconsidering a grouping when a scenario/horizon changes. The draft correctly\navoids claiming a general equivalence-deciding compiler, but does not specify\nenough supported transformations in its place.\n\nRequired evidence: define resolution metadata, state requirements and a small\nset of justified transformations. Include one grouping that preserves the\nrequested results and another that loses a rate, maturity or guarantee\nexposure. Declare the scope/error of approximate aggregation and retain its\nsource/detail references. Changing the query must trigger a sufficiency check.\n\n### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\n\n    try:post(s,changed,done);raise AssertionError('Expected identity error')\n    except ValueError as ex:check('event_identity_conflict',str(ex)=='EventIdentityConflict' and s['cash']==1,'Same ID different inputs rejected')\n    changed['id']='bad'\n    try:post(s,changed,done);raise AssertionError('Expected imbalance')\n    except ValueError as ex:check('atomic_rejection',str(ex)=='UnbalancedBatch' and s['cash']==1 and 'bad' not in done,'No partial state/journal mutation')\n\ndef QZ(x):\n    q=Q(x);return z3.RealVal(str(q.numerator)+'/'+str(q.denominator))\n\ndef bounds_and_weights():\n    f=load('borrowings.json');F,V=z3.Reals('rounded_F rounded_V');D=F+V\n    c=[F>=0,V>=0,D>=QZ('99.5'),D<QZ('100.5'),QZ('0.05')*D>=QZ('4.5'),QZ('0.05')*D<QZ('5.5')]\n    I=QZ('.05')*F+QZ('.07')*V;s=z3.Solver();s.add(*c)\n    for label,bound,comparison,attained in [('infimum','4.975',I<QZ('4.975'),True),('supremum','7.035',I>QZ('7.035'),False)]:\n        s.push();s.add(comparison);r=s.check();s.pop()\n        check('rounded_'+label+'_bound',r==z3.unsat,'Exact rational no-better-point certificate')\n        s.push();s.add(I==QZ(bound));r=s.check();s.pop()\n        check('rounded_'+label+'_attainment',(r==z3.sat)==attained,'Strict upper endpoint is not attained')\n    # A sequence approaching the open supremum establishes sharpness, alongside its bound proof.\n    for n in [10,100,1000]:\n        s.push();s.add(F==0,D==QZ('100.5')-QZ(Q(1,n)));r=s.check();s.pop()\n        check('upper_approach_'+str(n),r==z3.sat,'V = 100.5 - 1/n')\n    prior=list(map(Q,f['mixture']['prior']));lik=list(map(Q,f['mixture']['likelihood_new_evidence']))\n    mass=[a*b for a,b in zip(prior,lik)];postr=[x/sum(mass) for x in mass]\n    check('finite_bayes',postr==list(map(Q,f['mixture']['expected_posterior'])),'New evidence changes weights; stress selection alone does not')\n    check('joint_mixture',sum(w*x for w,x in zip(prior,[Q(5),Q(7)]))==Q('5.8'),'Mean from explicitly supplied weights only')\n    check('partial_mass',prior[0]+prior[1]==1 and prior[1]==Q('.4'),'Unresolved .4 retained; no unconditional mean computed')\n\ndef temporal():\n    f=load('temporal.json')\n    for i,q in enumerate(f['queries']):\n        eligible=[a for a in f['assertions'] if a['available']<=q['cutoff'] and (q.get('system_as_of') is None or a['ingested']<=q['system_as_of'])]\n        if q.get('mode')=='original':eligible=[a for a in eligible if not a['supersedes']]\n        else:\n            superseded={x for a in eligible for x in a['supersedes']};eligible=[a for a in eligible if a['id'] not in superseded]\n        check('temporal_query_'+str(i),{a['id'] for a in eligible}==set(q['expect']),q)\n    check('restated_half_year',Q('260')-Q('110')==Q(f['expected_valid_h2']),'Original H1 has incompatible vintage; its subtraction is not a current-view H2')\n\ndef sector_checks():\n    f=load('sectors.json');b=f['bank'];o={k:Q(v) for k,v in b['opening'].items()};e={k:Q(v) for k,v in b['events'].items()}\n    a=dict(cash=o['cash']-e['external_transfer']+e['loan_interest_cash'],gross_loans=o['gross_loans']+e['origination'],allowance=e['allowance_target'],deposits=o['deposits']+e['origination']-e['external_transfer']+e['deposit_interest_accrued'],equity=o['equity']+e['loan_interest_cash']-e['deposit_interest_accrued']-(e['allowance_target']-o['allowance']))\n    compare('bank_before_runoff',a,b['expected_before_runoff'])\n    check('bank_funding',max(Q(0),Q(b['runoff'])-a['cash'])==Q(b['expected_draw'])<=Q(b['facility_limit']),'Draw 4 to settle runoff 25')\n    check('bank_default_retained',Q(b['default_runoff'])-a['cash']-Q(b['facility_limit'])==Q(b['expected_unpaid']),'Unpaid 9 is an economic default outcome')\n    check('bank_capital',a['equity']-Q(b['regulatory_deduction'])==Q(b['expected_CET1']) and a['gross_loans']*Q(b['risk_weight'])==Q(b['expected_RWA']),'Illustrative prudential assumptions, no Basel compliance claim')\n    i=f['insurer'];v={k:Q(x) for k,x in i.items() if k!='expected'}\n    revenue=v['premium']*v['service_fraction']; expense=v['gross_claim_estimate']+v['gross_risk_adjustment']\n    recovery=v['gross_claim_estimate']*v['recovery_fraction']+v['ceded_risk_adjustment'];ceded_expense=v['ceded_premium']*v['service_fraction']\n    profit=revenue-expense-ceded_expense+recovery\n    a=dict(cash=v['opening_equity']+v['premium']-v['ceded_premium']-v['gross_claim_paid']+v['recovery_paid'],remaining_coverage_liability=v['premium']-revenue,incurred_claim_liability=expense-v['gross_claim_paid'],reinsurance_coverage_asset=v['ceded_premium']-ceded_expense,reinsurance_claim_asset=recovery-v['recovery_paid'],equity=v['opening_equity']+profit,profit=profit)\n    a['assets']=a['cash']+a['reinsurance_coverage_asset']+a['reinsurance_claim_asset'];a['liabilities']=a['remaining_coverage_liability']+a['incurred_claim_liability']\n    compare('insurance_rollforward',a,i['expected'])\n    check('insurance_balance',a['assets']==a['liabilities']+a['equity'],'Gross and ceded state remain separate')\n{\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"P03 remains limited to the declared Core0.1 debt profile.\",\n    \"Historical protected-file differences require documented attribution; they cannot justify ignoring new changes.\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    \"Audited baselines, proxy promotion, stop conditions, comparison fairness, hidden assumptions, stale recovery evidence, environment compatibility and artifact sufficiency.\",\n    \"Independently ran python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p03.py' -v: nine methods passed in 2.419 seconds.\",\n    \"Verified that all six contributed-file hashes match the existing conformance report.\",\n    \"Inspected independent typed/source comparisons, changed-input cases, schema-valid semantic rejection tests and unsupported-scope reporting.\",\n    \"Confirmed both temporary protection snapshots differ from current files at docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md, supporting the planned provenance repair.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"scripts/check_accounting_p03.py\",\n    \"scripts/core0_frontends_v1.py\",\n    \"scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\",\n    \"tests/test_accounting_p03.py\",\n    \"docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md\",\n    \"docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json\",\n    \"docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/conformance.json\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/progress.md\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03/approved-plan.json\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03/execution-1/changes.json\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/phase-entry-inventory.json\"\n  ],\n  \"issues\": [],\n  \"next_actions\": [\n    \"Repair checker provenance handling using durable, explicitly identified historical and current execution baselines. Missing protection evidence must not silently pass; missing or newly changed protected files must prevent acceptance.\",\n    \"Run the required suite and checker, preserving complete catalog observations and actual command, environment, timing, plan reference and file hashes.\",\n    \"Regenerate conformance.json and result.md, update progress.md, and submit the fresh outputs for result review.\"\n  ],\n  \"residuals\": [\n    \"This approves the repair plan, not the existing implementation result. The prior timed-out process and stale reports remain insufficient for acceptance.\",\n    \"The output-writing checker was not executed during this read-only review; its repaired behavior and fresh output integrity require verification.\",\n    \"General language, mapping and broader uncertainty support remain incomplete. G2, G12 and G15 remain open.\",\n    \"Accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, authoring superiority and human acceptance are not established.\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Checked the recovery snapshot against structured prior records and current files.\",\n    \"Verified that the remaining repair plan retains every original P03 criterion and addresses the identified provenance and reporting defects.\",\n    \"Completed a focused read-only verification without changing files.\"\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"AGREE. The bounded repair plan has no unresolved material objection. Current tests pass, and the proposed fresh execution and provenance repairs address the stale recovery evidence without weakening semantic acceptance or claiming broader completion.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"AGREE\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
