{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '177,227p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '1,120p' docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json; sed -n '1,75p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md; rg -n '\"'^def |''^class '\"' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py tests/test_accounting_p03.py\"","aggregated_output":"Supported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\nbounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\nMoney quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\nminor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\nand nonlinear constraints may not be silently submitted as continuous LPs.\nUnknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\nfunctions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\nFixed proportions times known totals are linear; variable F,V with F+V=D is\nlinear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\nproved D>0 becomes F>=aD; an unknown a restores bilinearity.\n\nFeasibility results are sat+exact witness, unsat+constraint/source core or\nunknown+reason+undecided formula. Bounds include lower/upper rational value,\nattainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ninequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\nunknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\ntimeout preserves undecided cells rather than deleting them.\n\n## Temporal selection and local review\n\nAn EvidenceView first filters by availability cutoff and (if requested)\ningestion cutoff. Day-only availability maps to the next local midnight using\nthe named timezone; finer availability requires evidence. Selective explicit\nsupersession removes only the targeted assertions in the same context. A\nsuperseding assertion must be eligible itself. Transitive successors follow\nthe acyclic supersession graph. Competing maximal assertions form a conflict\nset, never a last-row-wins result. Original view chooses initial assertions in\neach chain from a declared filing, not arbitrary earliest ingestion. A filing\nwith no prior version supplies its original itself. Harmonisation derives new\nobservations, preserves originals and records all transformation rules.\n\nIntervals are [start,end_exclusive) in a calendar; balance instants refer to\nthe end-of-day boundary. Cumulative subtraction requires same start, nested\nend, units/basis/perimeter and revision group, or an explicit compatibility\nassertion supported by review. A restatement of one flow does not restate every\nnote. Prospective estimate changes affect events from their effective date;\nretrospective corrections generate a new view and an explicit opening bridge.\n\nReview states are Proposed, Accepted, AcceptedAlternative, Rejected and\nSuperseded. Accept requires verified locator/literal, context, rationale,\nreviewer/date, applicability checks and a reconciliation result. Acceptance\nof an extraction is separate from acceptance of an accounting interpretation.\nSeveral accepted alternatives need a choice group. Reject never deletes source\nbytes. Correction creates a new reading linked to the old one; replacing an\naccepted reading requires a supersession action. An unresolved contradiction\nsets conflict, even if each extraction was accepted. No LLM confidence becomes\na hypothesis weight. Derived formulas, mappings, measurements and runs record\ndependency IDs; a changed decision makes their descendants stale for new\nviews. Historic frozen runs remain replayable, labelled with their old view.\n\n## Uncertainty, scenarios and results\n{\n  \"exact\": {\n    \"principal\": \"100\",\n    \"historical_rate\": \"0.05\",\n    \"historical_interest\": \"5\",\n    \"fixed_rate\": \"0.05\",\n    \"stress_rate\": \"0.07\",\n    \"cash\": \"95\",\n    \"equity\": \"-5\",\n    \"expected\": {\n      \"fixed_interest\": \"5\",\n      \"floating_interest\": \"7\",\n      \"fixed_cash\": \"90\",\n      \"floating_cash\": \"88\",\n      \"fixed_equity\": \"-10\",\n      \"floating_equity\": \"-12\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"rounded\": {\n    \"debt\": [\n      \"99.5\",\n      \"100.5\"\n    ],\n    \"interest\": [\n      \"4.5\",\n      \"5.5\"\n    ],\n    \"interval\": \"lower closed, upper open\",\n    \"constraints\": [\n      \"F>=0\",\n      \"V>=0\",\n      \"99.5<=F+V<100.5\",\n      \"4.5<=0.05*(F+V)<5.5\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_infimum\": \"4.975\",\n    \"expected_infimum_attained\": true,\n    \"expected_supremum\": \"7.035\",\n    \"expected_supremum_attained\": false\n  },\n  \"mixture\": {\n    \"hypotheses\": [\n      \"fixed\",\n      \"floating\"\n    ],\n    \"prior\": [\n      \"0.6\",\n      \"0.4\"\n    ],\n    \"likelihood_new_evidence\": [\n      \"0.2\",\n      \"0.8\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_posterior\": [\n      \"3/11\",\n      \"8/11\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_stress_mean\": \"5.8\",\n    \"partial_failure\": {\n      \"fixed\": \"complete\",\n      \"floating\": \"unsupported\",\n      \"successful_mass\": \"0.6\",\n      \"unresolved_mass\": \"0.4\",\n      \"unconditional_mean\": \"unavailable\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n# Core 0.1 debt source lowering, version 1\n\nThis executable profile supplements the protected Core 0 grammar and contract.\n`compile_source(text, bindings)` parses real source; `compile_program(Program,\nbindings)` accepts immutable typed declarations. Both bind names, check quantities\nand context, construct shared IR, and submit it to independent schema and semantic\nvalidation. Neither entrypoint reads the authored expected IR or expected results.\n\n## Execution evidence contract\n\nThe approved P03 plan remains the implementation boundary. Acceptance requires\nreal source lowering, independent typed/source equivalence, changed-input\nsensitivity, semantic rejection and complete catalog execution. The current\nimplementation preserves global constraints, explicit annual-rate units,\nacceptance records, package bindings and domain checks.\n\nThe baseline is `borrowing.acc`, plus documented corresponding fields of the\nauthored IR, whose reconstruction claims are excluded. Independently constructed\ntyped programs and exact arithmetic checks supplement agreement between frontends.\nSchema validity is a prerequisite, not semantic acceptance. Negative IR cases must\nbe structurally valid before testing the intended semantic rejection. Stops are\nunexpected protected-input changes, missing dependencies, or failing mandatory\nchecks; failures trigger repair, never a passing report. No statistical, timing,\nusability, accounting-compliance or forecasting comparison is being run.\n\nProvenance of material choices: exact rationals, lexical rules and quantities come\nfrom `core-contract.md`; USD accounts and DebtMix fields come from the local\nDemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\nThe single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\nmultiple-source reconciliation is unsupported. Synthetic acceptance and admission\nrecords are supplied by the caller. Absence of reconstruction requires Unknown\nfeasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched cell, no witnesses\nand no solver results. Early diagnostics cover unit loss, silent constraint loss,\ninvented acceptance and copied package digests. A pass establishes deterministic\nengineering conformance only. Results are preserved in the two P03 deliverables.\n\nThe writable project files are the two versioned modules, checker, required test,\nthis profile, the versioned cases JSON and the two P03 deliverables. Existing\ngrammar/schema, authored fixtures, legacy validators, controllers, release-pinned\nfiles and preserved snapshots remain protected. Recorded protected inputs are\nchecked against durable supervisor execution-entry hashes and before/after the\ncheck; historical phase-entry differences are separately attributed. Git is\nunavailable (existing marker is not a usable repository); no Git initialization.\nPython 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are existing dependencies. No\naccelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\nEquity roles respectively: the package report actually names these accounts.\nOther declaration names may vary. There may be multiple lets, Boolean constraints\nand conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nGlobal constraints constrain the parent family; alternative constraints stay in\ntheir respective branches and are not conjoined in the parent. No branch is\nselected or solved.\n\nBindings explicitly supply a digest-locked local package, synthetic reading and\nacceptance action, information/system cutoffs, opening balances, perimeter,\nsymbol admission, assumption periods/origins, and alternative authorship. Binding\nrecords remain separate from package definitions. Every acceptance must explicitly\nsay Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\nthe retained DemoDebt file and checks its fixed version, digest, exports and\napplicability. Paths escaping the repository and overrides are errors. The\npackage's registry examples and expected-result fields are not compiler inputs.\n\nDecimal tokens become Fraction directly; binary floats are rejected. Strings use\nJSON escapes, reject unpaired surrogates and normalize semantic strings to NFC.\nOriginal spelling and Unicode-code-point offsets remain in the separate source\nmap; typed locations identify constructors. LF, CRLF, comments and whitespace\npreserve semantics. Dates are Gregorian. All grammar words are reserved.\n\nExpressions include literals, shared references, `value(observation)`, unary minus,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:46:class _Failure(Exception):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:53:class Diagnostic:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:73:class CompileResult:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:90:class ValidationResult:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:99:def _pairs(value: Mapping[str, Any] | Iterable[tuple[str, Any]] | None) -> tuple[tuple[str, Any], ...]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:107:def _tuple(value: Iterable[Any] | None) -> tuple[Any, ...]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:111:def _fraction(value: Fraction | int | str | Decimal) -> Fraction:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:126:def rational(value: Fraction | int | str | Decimal) -> dict[str, str]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:131:def parse_rational(value: Mapping[str, str]) -> Fraction:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:144:def _clean_id(value: str) -> str:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:149:def _iso(value: str, where: str) -> str:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:159:def _string(value: str) -> str:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:165:def binding_projection(value: Any) -> Any:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:180:def _instant(value: str, where: str) -> str:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:190:def _time(kind: str, start: str, end: Optional[str], calendar: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:206:class Expr:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:211:class Literal(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:219:class Ref(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:224:class External(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:229:class Call(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:239:class Binary(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:246:class Unary(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:252:class ArrayExpr(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:260:class RecordExpr(Expr):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:268:class UseDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:274:class SourceDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:280:class EntityDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:286:class BookDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:294:class AccountDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:301:class OpeningDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:308:class ObservationDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:317:class SymbolDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:326:class LetDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:333:class ConstraintDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:339:class ContractDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:354:class AlternativeDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:364:class ScenarioDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:374:class ReportDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:381:class UnsupportedDecl:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:392:class Program:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:413:class ReadingBinding:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:437:class OpeningBinding:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:458:class ReportBinding:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:475:class PackageBinding:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:517:class AssumptionBinding:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:542:class SymbolAdmission:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:552:class AlternativeBinding:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:560:class CompileBindings:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:686:def _unique(rows, attr, key, code):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:693:def _validate_bindings(bindings: CompileBindings) -> None:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:823:def _empty_ir() -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:838:def _diag(code: str, message: str, location: str, capability: Optional[str] = None,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:843:class _Compiler:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1528:def _numeric_type(typ: str) -> bool:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1532:def _is_scalar(typ: str) -> bool:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1536:def _merge_context(left: Optional[str], right: Optional[str], owner: str, compiler: _Compiler) -> Optional[str]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1542:def _literal_value(expr: Expr, where: str) -> Any:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1550:def _arithmetic(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Any:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1564:def _compare(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1571:def _fold_bool(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1577:def compile_program(program: Program, bindings: CompileBindings,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1598:def _load_schema() -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1605:def _invalid(code: str, message: str, location: str) -> Diagnostic:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1609:def _nodes(ir: Mapping[str, Any]) -> tuple[dict[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], Optional[Diagnostic]]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1624:def _ref(nodes: Mapping[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], identifier: str,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1633:class _IRTypeChecker:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1770:def _expression_bounds(identifier, nodes):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1793:def validate_ir(ir: Mapping[str, Any], bindings: CompileBindings,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2076:def _validate_profile_integrity(ir, bindings, nodes, checker):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2144:class _Symbolic:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2148:def evaluate_expression(ir: Mapping[str, Any], identifier: str,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2201:def semantic_projection(ir: Mapping[str, Any] | None) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:45:def bindings(principal=100, renamed=False):\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:73:def typed(principal=100, stress=F(7,100), renamed=False, arithmetic=False):\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:102:def arithmetic_source():\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:137:class P03Tests(unittest.TestCase):\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:379:def expression(doc, suffix):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
