{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '228,270p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '138,162p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=json.loads(Path('docs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json').read_text())\nfor k in ('ModelScope','HistoryFamily','SolverResult','BoundResult'):\n d=p['\"'$defs'\"'].get(k)\n if d:\n  print(k,json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\nUncertainty kinds are ExtractionReading, HistoricalFact, AccountingElection,\nMeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy and FutureInnovation. Each has scope,\ndomain, evidence, dependencies and admission rule. An election needs a dated\npermitted treatment and evidence of eligibility; a balanced but prohibited\ntreatment is UnsupportedTreatment. Estimates need a method/date/inputs; future\ninnovations need a joint law and measure. New observations constrain facts;\ncorrections replace evidence views; likelihoods update probability models;\nhypothetical stresses alone do none of those.\n\nExogenousStress supplies named driver paths without updating historical weights.\nObservationalConditioning supplies observed events, a joint model and positive\nevent probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\nweights exactly. Zero probability yields UndefinedConditioning, not equal\nweights. Continuous density conditioning requires an explicit conditional\nmodel/regular conditional distribution adapter. StructuralIntervention replaces\nspecified equations in a named acyclic structural model, retaining exogenous\nnoise; absence of that model yields UnsupportedScenario. Risk-neutral pricing\nand real-world simulation measures have different IDs and cannot be mixed\nwithout an explicit justified transformation.\n\nInformationView(date, observer, role, evidence_view, committed_prefix,\nannounced_scenario_inputs, forecast_model) exposes past/current facts and\npermitted forecasts. Future realised innovations and future event outcomes\nare unavailable. A scenario may announce an entire stress path to management\nonly when its visibility is `announced`; otherwise management sees current and\npast driver values. Valuation uses an inner expectation conditional on this\nview, with an independent stream domain from outer realised defaults.\n\nRunResult preserves rows by hypothesis/continuous condition, scenario, path and\ndate. Cells carry Context and Exact/Symbolic/Samples/CertifiedBounds/ExploredRange/\nUnresolved tags. Path failure has an enum: EconomicDefault, Unsupported,\nNumericalFailure, SolverUnknown, Cancelled. Default retains the legal obligations\nand usable state; an unsupported required treatment stops affected descendants.\nUnaffected outputs may survive through the dependency graph. No unweighted\nfamily has a mean. Weighted runs preserve successful, unresolved and default\nmass; missing outcomes block unconditional means/quantiles. Conditional-on-success\nresults require an explicit separate request and show their denominator.\n\nFinite joint measures attach to disjoint economic hypotheses, not alternative\nlabels. Overlapping views cannot be summed; reparameterisations require a\npushforward measure, with Jacobian where densities are used. Priors and\nlikelihoods list information blocks so totals/components do not duplicate\n### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\n\nRequirements: MC11, MC22. Refines G1 and G6.\nEvidence: [conditional-law equivalence](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:222).\n\nThe definition that grouped histories must have the same relevant conditional\nlaws is useful. It does not supply a usable rule for choosing instrument,\nlot, vintage or cohort resolution, carrying necessary accounting memory, or\nreconsidering a grouping when a scenario/horizon changes. The draft correctly\navoids claiming a general equivalence-deciding compiler, but does not specify\nenough supported transformations in its place.\n\nRequired evidence: define resolution metadata, state requirements and a small\nset of justified transformations. Include one grouping that preserves the\nrequested results and another that loses a rate, maturity or guarantee\nexposure. Declare the scope/error of approximate aggregation and retain its\nsource/detail references. Changing the query must trigger a sufficiency check.\n\n### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\n\nRequirements: MC04, MC27. Refines G2, G5 and G10.\nEvidence: [review actions](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/09-implementation.tex:142)\nand [correction proposals](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:13).\n\nThe analyst can accept, reject, add an alternative or correct a proposal, but\nModelScope {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"templates\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"slot_limits\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldBinding\"}}, \"resolution\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"calendars\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"choices\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"exclusions\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"obligations\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"templates\", \"slot_limits\", \"resolution\", \"calendars\", \"choices\", \"exclusions\", \"obligations\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}\nHistoryFamily {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"scope\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence_view\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"opening_state\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"symbols\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"choices\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"constraints\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"alternatives\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"feasibility\": {\"enum\": [\"Feasible\", \"Infeasible\", \"Unknown\"]}, \"coverage\": {\"enum\": [\"ExactWithinScope\", \"PartialSearch\", \"Approximate\"]}, \"completed_cells\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0}, \"unresolved_cells\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0}, \"witnesses\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"solver_results\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"scope\", \"evidence_view\", \"opening_state\", \"symbols\", \"choices\", \"constraints\", \"alternatives\", \"feasibility\", \"coverage\", \"completed_cells\", \"unresolved_cells\", \"witnesses\", \"solver_results\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
