{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '270,302p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json; sed -n '1,52p' scripts/check_accounting_p03.py; sed -n '1,52p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md\"","aggregated_output":"likelihoods list information blocks so totals/components do not duplicate\nevidence. Exact finite inference is the reference optional method. Continuous\ninference requires a declared density/parameterisation, numerical validity,\nmultiple-chain/seed and downstream checks; no sampler default is selected here.\n\n## Identity, replay, migration and storage\n\nCanonical bytes are UTF-8 JSON, NFC strings, sorted ASCII keys, separators `,`/`:`\nwithout whitespace, no floats, NaN, duplicate keys or negative zero. All numeric\nvalues are reduced rational records. Arrays preserve order except schema fields\ndeclared sets: dependencies, source IDs and constraint conjunctions sort by ID.\nNo general algebraic equivalence rewriting is implied. Evidence identity hashes\nraw documents, locators, extraction/review versions and context. Model identity\nhashes normalised IR, assumptions, rule/calculator locks and resolution contract,\nexcluding source byte offsets/formatting. Run identity additionally hashes\nevidence view, scenarios, horizon, outputs, numeric/calendars, stream scheme and\nenvironment profile. Every digest is SHA-256 with a domain/version prefix.\n\nEvent ID hashes run-independent economic owner, schedule version, date, phase,\noperation and occurrence ordinal. Idempotency keys pair run ID and event ID;\nsame payload returns the committed result, changed payload yields conflict.\nIndependent events may reorder only if their read/write sets are disjoint or\nthe package proves commutation, including cash/funding constraints. Otherwise\nexplicit dependencies decide order or expose ambiguity. Atomic commit includes\neconomic state, journals, measurements and explanation edges.\n\nThe reference random primitive hashes the canonical tuple (stream-v1, seed,\ncoupling-group, entity, contract/cohort, economic-date, shock-kind, draw-index),\ntakes the first unsigned 64 bits in big-endian order, and maps to the open-unit\nrational (integer+1/2)/2^64. Branch enumeration order is absent. Coupling groups\ndeclare shared uniforms; marginal transforms and correlation construction are\nversioned. This is a deterministic reference primitive, not a claim of validated\nMonte Carlo quality. Research runs must name an assessed counter-based generator\n{\n  \"exact\": {\n    \"principal\": \"100\",\n    \"historical_rate\": \"0.05\",\n    \"historical_interest\": \"5\",\n    \"fixed_rate\": \"0.05\",\n    \"stress_rate\": \"0.07\",\n    \"cash\": \"95\",\n    \"equity\": \"-5\",\n    \"expected\": {\n      \"fixed_interest\": \"5\",\n      \"floating_interest\": \"7\",\n      \"fixed_cash\": \"90\",\n      \"floating_cash\": \"88\",\n      \"fixed_equity\": \"-10\",\n      \"floating_equity\": \"-12\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"rounded\": {\n    \"debt\": [\n      \"99.5\",\n      \"100.5\"\n    ],\n    \"interest\": [\n      \"4.5\",\n      \"5.5\"\n    ],\n    \"interval\": \"lower closed, upper open\",\n    \"constraints\": [\n      \"F>=0\",\n      \"V>=0\",\n      \"99.5<=F+V<100.5\",\n      \"4.5<=0.05*(F+V)<5.5\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_infimum\": \"4.975\",\n    \"expected_infimum_attained\": true,\n    \"expected_supremum\": \"7.035\",\n    \"expected_supremum_attained\": false\n  },\n  \"mixture\": {\n    \"hypotheses\": [\n      \"fixed\",\n      \"floating\"\n    ],\n    \"prior\": [\n      \"0.6\",\n      \"0.4\"\n    ],\n    \"likelihood_new_evidence\": [\n      \"0.2\",\n      \"0.8\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_posterior\": [\n      \"3/11\",\n      \"8/11\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_stress_mean\": \"5.8\",\n    \"partial_failure\": {\n      \"fixed\": \"complete\",\n      \"floating\": \"unsupported\",\n      \"successful_mass\": \"0.6\",\n      \"unresolved_mass\": \"0.4\",\n      \"unconditional_mean\": \"unavailable\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Execute catalogued P03 obligations with durable protection provenance.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport hashlib\nimport io\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport platform\nimport re\nimport shlex\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport unittest\nfrom importlib.metadata import version\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nCHANGED = ['scripts/core0_frontends_v1.py', 'scripts/core0_ir_v1.py',\n           'scripts/check_accounting_p03.py', 'tests/test_accounting_p03.py',\n           'docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md',\n           'docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json']\nOUTPUTS = ['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/' + name\n           for name in ('conformance.json', 'result.md', 'progress.md')]\nPHASE_FILES = CHANGED + OUTPUTS\nPHASE_INVENTORY = 'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/phase-entry-inventory.json'\nEXECUTION_INVENTORY = 'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json'\nAPPROVED_PLAN = 'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P03/approved-plan.json'\n\n\ndef digest(path):\n    try:\n        return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n\n\ndef _unique_object(pairs):\n    result = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in result:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate inventory key: ' + key)\n        result[key] = value\n    return result\n\n\ndef _inventory(root, relative):\n    path = Path(relative)\n    if path.is_absolute() or '..' in path.parts or path.as_posix() != relative:\n        raise ValueError('inventory path must be repository-relative')\n    data = json.loads((root / path).read_text(), object_pairs_hook=_unique_object)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict) or not data:\n# Core 0.1 debt source lowering, version 1\n\nThis executable profile supplements the protected Core 0 grammar and contract.\n`compile_source(text, bindings)` parses real source; `compile_program(Program,\nbindings)` accepts immutable typed declarations. Both bind names, check quantities\nand context, construct shared IR, and submit it to independent schema and semantic\nvalidation. Neither entrypoint reads the authored expected IR or expected results.\n\n## Execution evidence contract\n\nThe approved P03 plan remains the implementation boundary. Acceptance requires\nreal source lowering, independent typed/source equivalence, changed-input\nsensitivity, semantic rejection and complete catalog execution. The current\nimplementation preserves global constraints, explicit annual-rate units,\nacceptance records, package bindings and domain checks.\n\nThe baseline is `borrowing.acc`, plus documented corresponding fields of the\nauthored IR, whose reconstruction claims are excluded. Independently constructed\ntyped programs and exact arithmetic checks supplement agreement between frontends.\nSchema validity is a prerequisite, not semantic acceptance. Negative IR cases must\nbe structurally valid before testing the intended semantic rejection. Stops are\nunexpected protected-input changes, missing dependencies, or failing mandatory\nchecks; failures trigger repair, never a passing report. No statistical, timing,\nusability, accounting-compliance or forecasting comparison is being run.\n\nProvenance of material choices: exact rationals, lexical rules and quantities come\nfrom `core-contract.md`; USD accounts and DebtMix fields come from the local\nDemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\nThe single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\nmultiple-source reconciliation is unsupported. Synthetic acceptance and admission\nrecords are supplied by the caller. Absence of reconstruction requires Unknown\nfeasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched cell, no witnesses\nand no solver results. Early diagnostics cover unit loss, silent constraint loss,\ninvented acceptance and copied package digests. A pass establishes deterministic\nengineering conformance only. Results are preserved in the two P03 deliverables.\n\nThe writable project files are the two versioned modules, checker, required test,\nthis profile, the versioned cases JSON and the two P03 deliverables. Existing\ngrammar/schema, authored fixtures, legacy validators, controllers, release-pinned\nfiles and preserved snapshots remain protected. Recorded protected inputs are\nchecked against durable supervisor execution-entry hashes and before/after the\ncheck; historical phase-entry differences are separately attributed. Git is\nunavailable (existing marker is not a usable repository); no Git initialization.\nPython 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are existing dependencies. No\naccelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
