{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"P04 is a new implementation slice: all three required files are absent, and the recovery record contains no prior P04 attempt or review findings. This planning pass changes no files.\",\n    \"Use existing Python, fractions.Fraction and Z3; record their actual versions. Exact rationals and bounded solver scope come from core-contract.md. Z3 is available, but its answers require independent checks; it is an implementation choice, not a promoted numerical default.\",\n    \"Support explicit, caller-supplied template registries, finite slot declarations, context-compatible observations and rational-linear state/report mappings. Automated disclosure interpretation, arbitrary template discovery and full accounting execution remain outside this slice.\",\n    \"P03's Core0.1 validator deliberately requires unsearched history families and rejects finite choices. Consume validated P03 inputs through a new adapter and return a separate versioned reconstruction result; preserve the accepted compiler, schema and evidence.\",\n    \"Every request must explicitly declare integer bounds, rounding convention/stage, evidence view, query scope and resource limits. Unknown conventions remain unresolved. Small fixture sizes and budgets are engineering test choices, not production defaults.\",\n    \"Implementation requires an authorised writable execution environment. This planner is read-only; no approval or sandbox bypass is requested.\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    \"Run python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p04.py' -v. Require every catalogued obligation to execute, with no failures, errors, skips, duplicate IDs or missing observations.\",\n    \"Compare complete feasible assignment sets for small bounded integer/finite-choice models against an independently written Fraction-based enumerator that replays original templates and observations without cal